      <h2 id="plan-yours">How to plan your own tiny house layout</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Size it</h3><p>Use the <a href="/tools/how-big-should-my-tiny-house-be/">size calculator</a> to set a square footage for your household.</p></li>
        <li><h3>List the must-haves</h3><p>Main-floor bedroom or loft, tub or shower, washer, desk, guest bed. Rank them.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Sketch at scale</h3><p>Drag rooms and furniture into the <a href="/tools/tiny-house-layout-planner/">tiny house layout planner</a> and walk through a typical day.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Match it to a plan</h3><p>Compare your sketch to <a href="/tiny-house-plans/">our tiny house plans</a>, or ask Tiny Homes Blueprint to modify one.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p>Once you have a layout you like, price it with the <a href="/tools/tiny-house-cost-calculator/">cost calculator</a> and check what your county allows in the <a href="/blog/tiny-house-zoning-laws/">tiny house zoning laws guide</a>. If you are building on a trailer, start with <a href="/tiny-house-on-wheels-plans/">tiny house on wheels plans</a> designed around road limits. If you are building from scratch, <a href="/blog/how-to-build-a-tiny-house/">how to build a tiny house</a> covers the steps from layout to finished home.</p>

